course: dictionary
lesson: 9425
title: Two letters, many meanings: ss
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The letters ss can mean different things. The words around them are the context, and they tell you which meaning you need. «The SS Great Britain was a famous steamship.» Here SS is short for steamship, because it stands before a ship's name.
explain: In a spelling word, ss is just a double s, as in miss, class and kiss. «Roots ending in ss take -ssion: discuss, discussion.» The root keeps its double s and then adds the ending, so the spelling of the root stays the same.
explain: In an online chat, ss can mean screenshot. If a friend writes «Send me an ss of the score!», they mean a picture of the screen. Always ask: is this a ship, a spelling, or a chat? The clues will tell you.
fact: ss is a double letter in many words, such as miss, class and kiss.
fact: SS before a ship's name stands for steamship, as in the SS Great Britain, a famous early ship.
fact: Ss is short for Saints in church names, as in Ss Peter and Paul.
fact: The Nazi SS was a violent military and police force in Germany during the Second World War. It ran concentration camps and carried out the Holocaust, a terrible crime against millions of people. Talk about it with your teacher, because it is serious and true.
fact: The floss rule: f, l, s and z are often doubled at the end of short words after one short vowel, as in off, fill, miss and buzz.
exercise: «The SS Great Britain sailed across the Atlantic.» In this sentence, what does SS stand for? | Saints | Screenshot | *Steamship
exercise: A friend writes in chat, «Send me an ss of that level.» What does ss mean here? | *Screenshot | Steamship | Saints | Double letter in a spelling word
exercise: Which word has a double s? | bag | sun | bed | *miss
test: Church names like «Ss Peter and Paul» use Ss. What does Ss stand for? | Stones | *Saints | Sailors | Sisters
test: «Roots ending in ss take -ssion: express, expression.» What is the root word in expression? | *express | expert | expression | sion
exam: Ben reads «The SS Great Britain was a famous steamship.» Later he sees «Ss Peter and Paul» in a church book. What does Ss mean in the church name? | Double letter in a spelling word | Screenshot | *Saints | Steamship
